      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(line): cap user profile cache",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an unbounded in-process **`userProfileCache`** in the LINE send path. Profile lookups are cached for 5 minutes but had no size cap, so gateways serving many distinct LINE users could grow memory without limit.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nExtracts `cacheLineUserProfile` and applies `pruneMapToMaxSize` after each write, capped at **1 024 entries** with LRU eviction.\n\n## User Impact\n\nLong-lived LINE gateways get bounded profile-cache memory. Behavior is unchanged for the first 1 024 distinct cached users within the TTL window.\n\n## Evidence\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs run extensions/line/src/send.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n```\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Behavior or issue addressed:** LINE user profile cache grew without bound under high distinct-user volume.\n- **Real environment tested:** macOS (Darwin arm64), Node.js v22.22.0, local source checkout on branch `fix/line-cap-user-profile-cache`.\n- **Exact steps or command run after this patch:**\n  1. `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run extensions/line/src/send.test.ts --reporter=verbose`\n- **Evidence after fix:**\n\n```text\n ✓ evicts oldest profile cache entries once the cache exceeds its cap\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  16 passed (16)\n```\n\n- **Observed result after fix:** After 1 025 profile fetches the oldest cached user is evicted and the next lookup re-fetches from the API mock; newest entries remain cached.\n- **What was not tested:** Live LINE Messaging API profile fetch.\n",
        "branch": "fix/line-cap-user-profile-cache",
